9cddd19ec70276" :answer/id #uuid "b0c8242d-072c-514c-9c4c-73a2cd629c7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x<-2$ or    $x>3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-144430/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90ca2d34-4b6f-5ce5-bfd8-4c436356a2cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-144430/selection/8ebe1ab94735904f6c890cb18de082421b88043077f9fcac5fd1a99fd159235f" :answer-field/choices ["q-144430/selection/8ebe1ab94735904f6c890cb18de082421b88043077f9fcac5fd1a99fd159235f" "q-144430/selection/484e812303ee353ae1663939df8cb7ca05a0e6231316bbff2ba5d3142f11caaf" "q-144430/selection/7d5a79da194ee7d3a542dd6bc2cebdf81c21f015ca430e787588d16d77d01aef" "q-144430/selection/116d233a36a47dbf616a37e6eb4e2a3f3301c2f5d5050b1642a18a316ed9b45f" "q-144430/selection/ad3bb82b390f715cb7c3dd284498de0eee6f46551dd7c5a83a9cddd19ec70276"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-144430" :question/id #uuid "3d8df1a8-f5cf-51ba-9094-39450d19c1c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-144430" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/eb5f5bfa7f1ead4caa0abd6394903b572cf973ae15759a8b627b1ce4f02cc3a7.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $6+x-{x}^{2}>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n6+x-{x}^{2}>0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny=6+x-{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/40fea084b16f1bf9b1274351377d7608e5f2b505eecc81c5dc23a6fc30edb77b.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-144430/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eec195c-6549-5de2-b3f0-0417e5f518e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-144430"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5061"] :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $(x+2)(1-x) \\geq 0.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/f1beeeb1247e21e6ebf442f8f9171320674d760551fe715afa98047be78db2bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+2)(1-x) \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny = (x+2)(1-x)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/ae3c40faa7e89979c135c06adf944aa46ec01564c556becaea725412d3b2560c.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2 \\leq x \\leq 1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9975"] :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0.$    \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/93fa79fb8411a6bdf16b3eb9c1aab489377a9b0d039b0be4b884f8cdc47bf683.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny =-x^2+2x+3\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/6b11e0ab1c3cd92003d3b5330b4eab64e192efbe1953cfbc560b717ccc0e3c57.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -1$ or $x \\geq 3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9976"] :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-(x+2)(x-1) <  0.$      \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/c764652658e603142d22e4a9ec02c59c2143bd4d5df2a38d6d6e7dd629ccf88b.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x+2)(x-1) <   0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny = -(x+2)(x-1)\n$$\n\n   \n\nis *below* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/cb3adba60c427e4f68bf756301a9b101ce17ca32adb8ea6ba9f3b492cccce2cc.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x<    -2$ or    $x >  1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9935"] :question/problem "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $x^2- 3x-10 >0.$    \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/bb4b28c1fbc4e166f22acf62ae4ab11cdab0ee07c2c4af080db0bf7e290744aa.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\nx^2 -3x -10> 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola  \n\n$$\ny =x^2 -3x -10\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/ca22e171b36e21802769e3612a163d29b01209af1ef75887a65ab6013bb1401a.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x < -2$ or $x >   5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
